<SCENARIO VER="105">
{PLAYSND "システム音\The_Lampe.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\イラスト\立木三日2.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "300" "" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{CREATECG "プレート" "グラフィック\システム\立木三日プレート.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "180" "380" "600" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\イラスト\立木三日.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>Thank you for your hard work, <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama. With this, the Jusatsu Arc [Killing by Curse] is entirely over.<PG>
With the Jusatsu Arc [Killing by Curse] alone, a great deal is still unclear, and it is hard to say that even the Motoki-cho case has been solved.<PG>
Even so, the sight of them striving to learn the truth is truly valiant.<PG>
However, every ending has been one in which Natsumi Kogori, Haruka Niimura or Erina Goto is murdered, or else goes missing―<PG>
How can the three of them come back from this incident alive and unharmed―? For that, they themselves need to know the deeper parts of the incident.<PG>
Now then, from here on, let us change the point of view drastically.<PG>
Yes, we will look at this incident through the eyes of Haruka Niimura, the only one of the main characters who has had no subjective point of view.<PG>
Now then, I will guide you. Please behold their deeper karma, which could not be known in the Jusatsu Arc [Killing by Curse].<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "立木三日" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\イラスト\立木三日2.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
<PG>
{}
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
